# Cell path tracer

A Cell Broadband Engine port of Kevin Beason's smallpt path tracer. The PPU
program starts SPE workers, which trace four rays at a time with SPU SIMD
instructions. The default output size is 640 x 480; the Docker build helper
can override it for small simulator tests.

This repository is a historical source snapshot. The
checked-in `5000spp_forwardSPUSIMD_640x480.ppm` is an example image. See
[`CODE_REVIEW.md`](CODE_REVIEW.md) for the fixes and SIMD xoshiro128++ design.
For a tested x86_64 Docker image that provides the Cell
cross compilers and boots Cell Linux, see
[`EMULATION.md`](EMULATION.md).

## Requirements

- A PowerPC Cell system with SPEs and a Cell Linux environment.
- A PPU C compiler, `spu-gcc`, SPU SIMD math headers, `libspe2`, and pthreads.

Ordinary x86 or ARM GCC cannot compile the SPU source or run the resulting
program. The combined Docker image cross-compiles both project sources; the
PPU and SPU builds and small test renders completed in the simulator.

## Build and render in Docker

Build the combined SDK and simulator image as described in
[`EMULATION.md`](EMULATION.md), then run from this repository:

```sh
CELL_WIDTH=16 CELL_HEIGHT=12 bash docker/build-project.sh
bash docker/run-render.sh 4 1 12345
bash docker/test-rng.sh
```

The first command puts `forwardFloatSPU` and `smallptPPU` in `build/`. The
second runs four samples per pixel on one SPE with seed `12345` and writes
`build/image.ppm`. The seed argument is optional and defaults to `1`. The
third command runs the SPU RNG known-output test in the simulator.
The `build/` directory is ignored by Git. The render script refuses to
overwrite an existing image; move or rename it before another run. Omit the
width and height variables to build at the default 640 x 480 resolution.
The simulator is slow, so use a small size for functional tests. Image
quality still needs comparison with a high-sample scalar reference.
The renderer now samples the light directly at diffuse surfaces, making
low-sample previews show the room. For a less blocky preview, move the old
`build/image.ppm`, then build at `CELL_WIDTH=64 CELL_HEIGHT=48` and run
`bash docker/run-render.sh 16 2`. The checked-in example has 100 times as many
pixels and 312.5 times as many samples per pixel as that preview. Producing an
equivalent full render in the simulator is therefore a much larger job.

A 64 x 48 render at 5,000 samples per pixel completed with two SPE workers and
seed `1` in the simulator in about 14 hours 55 minutes on the tested x86_64
host. To reproduce it in a separate ignored build directory:

```sh
CELL_BUILD_DIR=build/render-5000-64x48 CELL_WIDTH=64 CELL_HEIGHT=48 \
  bash docker/build-project.sh
CELL_BUILD_DIR=build/render-5000-64x48 bash docker/run-render.sh 5000 2 1
```

The result is `build/render-5000-64x48/image.ppm`. It appears smoother than
the checked-in example, which shows grain and repeating ripples, but the two
images have different resolutions. Downsampling the 640 x 480 example to
64 x 48 gives a mean absolute RGB difference of 14.45; the new image remains
systematically brighter. See [CODE_REVIEW.md](CODE_REVIEW.md) for the measured
comparison and its limits.

## Intended build and use

Run from the repository directory:

```sh
spu-gcc -O3 forwardFloat-spu.c -o forwardFloatSPU -lm
gcc -Wall -m64 -maltivec -pthread smallpt-ppu.c -o smallptPPU -lspe2
./smallptPPU 48 6
```

On an x86_64 cross-build host, use the SDK's PPU cross compiler (`ppu-gcc`)
instead of host `gcc`. The resulting PPU executable runs in a Cell Linux
guest or on Cell hardware, not on the build host.

The first argument requests samples per pixel; the program requires a positive
multiple of four and traces four rays per iteration. The second argument
is the number of SPE workers, from one to six. An optional third argument sets
the 64-bit RNG seed. The program looks for `./forwardFloatSPU` and writes
an ASCII PPM (`P3`) file named `image.ppm` in the current directory, replacing
any existing file with that name.

## Source layout

- `smallpt-ppu.c`: PPU launcher, shared output buffer, SPE scheduling, and
  PPM writer.
- `forwardFloat-spu.c`: SPU SIMD ray traversal, shading, and DMA transfers.
- `spu-rng.h`: four-lane xoshiro128++ RNG and per-pixel stream seeding.
- `5000spp_forwardSPUSIMD_640x480.ppm`: checked-in example output.

## Validation status

The review fixes and RNG implementation are recorded in
[`CODE_REVIEW.md`](CODE_REVIEW.md). The SIMD RNG passed known-output tests in
the Cell guest, and the 5,000-sample render completed successfully.
Rendered-image accuracy and performance have not been measured against a
scalar reference or real Cell hardware.
